    "body": "That's a good question. That's something I missed bringing up in https://github.com/WICG/priority-hints/issues/24 as I was looking for more complicated examples. I'm not really sure about that one honestly, and I'm sure we can find even more complicated situations than that. It sounds like we shouldn't do trickle-down request prioritization for requests made within scripts (for consistency and ease of adoption), would you agree?\r\n\r\n### Edit\r\n\r\nSince accessing `document.currentScript` in that example from within the `lala` function would yield the script without `importance`, I guess there'd be no `importance` to trickle down in that case, but I'm really not sure if that's a good idea, or helps us out at all.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
